{title: Crown Him with Many Crowns}
{artist: Matthew Bridges / Godfrey Thring / George Elvey}
{genre: Hymn}
{flow: Opening}
{style: Traditional}
{key: D}
{tempo: 84}
{time: 4/4}
{key_original: Eb}
{score: crown-him-with-many-crowns.abc}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[D]Crown Him with many [G]crowns
The [D]Lamb upon His [A]throne
[D]Hark! how the heavenly [Bm]anthem drowns
[G]All music but its [A]own
A[D]wake, my soul, and [G]sing
Of [D]Him who died for [A]thee
And [Bm]hail Him as thy [G]matchless King
Through [A]all e[D]ternity
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[D]Crown Him the Lord of [G]life
Who [D]triumphed o'er the [A]grave
[D]Who rose victorious [Bm]in the strife
[G]For those He came to [A]save
His [D]glories now we [G]sing
Who [D]died, and rose on [A]high
Who [Bm]died eternal [G]life to bring
And [A]lives that death may [D]die
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[D]Crown Him the Lord of [G]love
Be[D]hold His hands and [A]side
[D]Rich wounds, yet visible [Bm]above
[G]In beauty glori[A]fied
No [D]angel in the [G]sky
Can [D]fully bear that [A]sight
But [Bm]downward bends his [G]burning eye
At [A]mysteries so [D]bright
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[D]Crown Him the Lord of [G]peace
Whose [D]power a scepter [A]sways
[D]From pole to pole, that [Bm]wars may cease
[G]And all be prayer and [A]praise
His [D]reign shall know no [G]end
And [D]round His pierced [A]feet
[Bm]Fair flowers of Para[G]dise extend
Their [A]fragrance ever [D]sweet
{end_of_verse}
